From 188c26896cf93a8bbbf427b428798bcb2158e67f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riotashley81-jpg <riotashley81@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:01:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Render passes: in-between images reach the screen; several
 pass workers

Presents of a pass generation were timed from the interval that promoted
it, one VBlank before the frame start the passes were planned for: the
first present already read phase 0.5 and showed the in-between image, the
next held it, and the game's own frame never reached the screen (image
pairs A' A' B' B'). Generations now keep the plan's frame start and length
and are presented by them.

The planner placed frames with the guest's 59.94 Hz VBlank length while a
presenter locked to the display runs whole refreshes, so the deadlines
drifted until they read as phase 0.998; and a deadline at the frame's end
(which shows the next game frame) was planned as an in-between image. The
plan now uses the schedule's own VBlank length and skips the frame's end.

Pass worker: psx_mod_pass_worker_start(count) runs up to 4 helper
processes, slot-addressed, so a title can build several in-between frames
of one game frame at once. A result is now read only for its own job
sequence (a stale done event made about 2% of single-helper results, and
40% with three, read as failed), helpers starting together no longer race
on the mod state file (per-process temp name), and failures carry a reason
(pass_worker_stats failed_why).

psx_mod_render_pass_present_slack_ms and psx_mod_set_render_pass_present_hook
let a title add late passes right before the present they are due for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
